{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology","id":1229954,"title":"If you could Revise CWOD Cosmology","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-25T01:30:16-07:00","id":1229954,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> If you could Revise CWOD Cosmology","content":"So if you could revise the Cosmology of the Classic World of Darkness, like your own directed reboot how would you go about changing things?<br /> <br /> Me personally I think it would be better if you condensed most of the Otherworldy dimensions. If it was a brand new setting I would experiment with the land of the dead being the same spirit world as the land of Nature spirits. But for the World of Darkness they would like room to concentrate ghost stories on Ghosts, so I would have the Dark Umbra be its own things, but like Yin Realms in the Middle Kingdom setting I would have it closer to the other spirit worlds. But I would condense the Penumbra, Dreaming and Astral into the same layer of existence. So Chimera would be spirits, animism and dream spirits interact and have shared ecology and possibly origins. When Vampires Astral Project they go here. But the Astral realms like that Vulgate River can still be accessed as its own area towards the Near Umbra Layer. Arcadia is in the Deep Umbra. No more issues with the Nunnehi or Hsien or even Inanimae existing along with other weird spirits and elementals. This would simplify a lot without really removing vital portions of the narrative, in fact I feel it will add a lot of depths when you can explore the nature of reality and spirits when both myth effects the spiritual landscape but somethings are always there.<br /> <br /> The Deep Umbra/Deep Dreaming are also on the very periphery of the Universe. They are on the outermost layer, with the Dreaming on the Wyld Layer that is the portion that stretches off into other Universes. Thus some Gods or beings like the Fomorians may have Trodded from elsewhere or may have vamoosed off to another universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T06:32:48-07:00","id":1229998,"title":"","content":"NWoD approach to cosmology, pretty much. Importance is to make the world feel like you don't know everything and things can't be put into neat boxes on what each creature is. I have used NWoD creatures in non-dice games, because they have a good variation of things and don't need to be attached to anything else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T07:38:24-07:00","id":1230017,"title":"","content":"I agree. The one thing I love in NWoD over CWoD is the Cthulhuesque feeling of the Unknown. The God-Machine itself is an excellent example of it.<br /> CWoD, as written, does not hold many suprises; Everything is explained, everything is a Spirit, a Fomor, a..well, you name it. Mostly, everything is a Spirit, or something that has been influenced by one of the big splats.<br /> <br /> Now, it is of course absolutely possible to go this route of the Unknown in CWoD - and it's not hard to do so simply through St creativity and freedom.<br /> But official-Fluff-wise, there simply is not much left as a mystery. Mage probably comes closest, with its many possibilities for high Umbrood, but again that runs into a well defined categorization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T08:19:47-07:00","id":1230020,"title":"","content":"Each game would have its own special place, it may even be redundant with other things but it will stick out. There will be an explicitly chaotic mess of contradictions and impossibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T09:46:05-07:00","id":1230036,"title":"","content":"The good thing about the cWoD is the pure amount of fluff and stuff you can use. There are so many supplements for so many games, there's always something you don't already know.<br /> The bad thing is, it is so much and so spread out, you can search for hours and hours until you find what you need.<br /> <br /> I don't like how NWoD approaches it's cosmology, creatures and &quot;gods&quot; with the whole &quot;you can't understand&quot; thing. The important part in M:tAs is that your character can't possibly know everything, because everything he knows somehow fits or forms his paradigm and there's always a different explanation that could also be true. In NWoD it's the fact that nobody can possibly understand a single creature because it's... not understandable? It just feels kind of cheap to me.<br /> Of course you want to be confronted with the unknown when you're playing the game. It's hard to forget these parts if you're a player and you recognize a certain being. It's a personal preference, really.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't change much about cWoDs comsology. Maybe a few books to condense the very great amount of information about the different worlds into more accessible form. That's what I would want. Then again, Werewolfs will meet different spirits than Vampires and Mages, so we will be having books for each game anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","user":"TheVarulfen","date":". 06-25-2018, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T10:26:31-07:00","id":1230042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230036#post1230036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The good thing about the cWoD is the pure amount of fluff and stuff you can use. There are so many supplements for so many games, there's always something you don't already know.<br /> The bad thing is, it is so much and so spread out, you can search for hours and hours until you find what you need.<br /> <br /> I don't like how NWoD approaches it's cosmology, creatures and &quot;gods&quot; with the whole &quot;you can't understand&quot; thing. The important part in M:tAs is that your character can't possibly know everything, because everything he knows somehow fits or forms his paradigm and there's always a different explanation that could also be true. In NWoD it's the fact that nobody can possibly understand a single creature because it's... not understandable? It just feels kind of cheap to me.<br /> Of course you want to be confronted with the unknown when you're playing the game. It's hard to forget these parts if you're a player and you recognize a certain being. It's a personal preference, really.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't change much about cWoDs comsology. Maybe a few books to condense the very great amount of information about the different worlds into more accessible form. That's what I would want. Then again, Werewolfs will meet different spirits than Vampires and Mages, so we will be having books for each game anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, NWoD's method works because it was build from ground up to leave enough 'holes' in the setting for the races to exist or not exist. Most likely, because crossover in cWoD is a huge mess, because the gamelines went their own ways, but referenced each other, but were separate, etc.<br /> <br /> To use a weird allegory, cWoD is like piling a bunch of fantasy books on to of one another, it is dense and the more you have to make sure it doesn't fall over. NWoD is like legos, sure you can build it like the instructions, or you can build what you like. I love the setting of cWoD a lot, but I prefer the looser worldbuilding since it is easier to wing things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T15:56:59-07:00","id":1230113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230036#post1230036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The good thing about the cWoD is the pure amount of fluff and stuff you can use. There are so many supplements for so many games, there's always something you don't already know.<br /> The bad thing is, it is so much and so spread out, you can search for hours and hours until you find what you need.<br /> <br /> I don't like how NWoD approaches it's cosmology, creatures and &quot;gods&quot; with the whole &quot;you can't understand&quot; thing. The important part in M:tAs is that your character can't possibly know everything, because everything he knows somehow fits or forms his paradigm and there's always a different explanation that could also be true. In NWoD it's the fact that nobody can possibly understand a single creature because it's... not understandable? It just feels kind of cheap to me.<br /> Of course you want to be confronted with the unknown when you're playing the game. It's hard to forget these parts if you're a player and you recognize a certain being. It's a personal preference, really..</div> </div> </div> </div>And I find the attempts people try to make Classic WOD understandable makes it cheap. Kindred keep better records across thousands of years than humanity? They NEVER lie? Werewolf Oral Culture perfectly records things? A world where reality litterally changes can have a simple understandable truth rather than it only being part of a bigger whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T06:25:15-07:00","id":1230260,"title":"","content":"I think the problem it's not the attempts of &quot;the people&quot;, but rather the attempts of some authors:<br /> <br /> No, of course you can't enter Hollow Earth without magick and you will disembody if you go to live there, it isn't part of the material world you silly.<br /> <br /> Your Paradigm may say Spirit are aliens, but they will use Spirit Traits and live in the Umbra anyway - of course you will turn into a spirit if you go live with them - similarities with the Hollow Earth and the Spirit Worlds are mere coincidence?.<br /> <br /> If Everything it's Real, then Nothing is...and thus everything out there can be sumarized as a bland splat that uses the same rules for everything, like Mage's Umbrood and Umbra show.<br /> <br /> Really, right now the Dreaming it's the only thing that doesn't fall neatly on the Umbra-model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T14:42:28-07:00","id":1230371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230260#post1230260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem it's not the attempts of &quot;the people&quot;, but rather the attempts of some authors:<br /> <br /> No, of course you can't enter Hollow Earth without magick and you will disembody if you go to live there, it isn't part of the material world you silly.<br /> <br /> Your Paradigm may say Spirit are aliens, but they will use Spirit Traits and live in the Umbra anyway - of course you will turn into a spirit if you go live with them - similarities with the Hollow Earth and the Spirit Worlds are mere coincidence?.<br /> <br /> If Everything it's Real, then Nothing is...and thus everything out there can be sumarized as a bland splat that uses the same rules for everything, like Mage's Umbrood and Umbra show.<br /> <br /> Really, right now the Dreaming it's the only thing that doesn't fall neatly on the Umbra-model.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the Dreaming is just another Umbra. I'd argue the Digital web more readily moves from the Pen/near/middle/far model","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T06:32:40-07:00","id":1230522,"title":"","content":"I think you're right about the Dreaming, albeit the books say it isn't a Zone nor one of the three worlds, it still follows the same general model for the Umbra. It could easily be called the 4 World (Dark, Wild, Astral, and now Dreaming).<br /> <br /> But the digital web?. With its data spiders, it's meme spirits, its virus spirits...I don't think so. I can locate the Web precisely as a well defined Zone of the Umbra located arround the Cyberrealm. Much like the Dream-Zone it's in the Astral Umbra regardless of the fact that humans enter there in their dreams. The only diference was that in First edition the Web was made of Forces instead of Spirit - but that was forgotten in 2.0<br /> <br /> I think that Zones (all of them) had a lot of potential as oddities that don't fall neatly on the Umbra model. But it was wasted. The difference was never explored and they (yes, including the Digital Web) were populated by Spirits and human emanations - which it's the whole complaint about Umbrood (that there's nothing more than spirits or splats to play with)<br /> <br /> The Dark Umbra sometimes gets interesting. Wraith insinuated that it, perhaps, was a reflection of the Wraith's own psyche - a personal travel as much an interpresonal world. But most of the time it's just a gloomy demiplane like the rest of the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-27-2018, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T13:22:54-07:00","id":1230627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230522#post1230522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the digital web?. With its data spiders, it's meme spirits, its virus spirits...I don't think so. I can locate the Web precisely as a well defined Zone of the Umbra located arround the Cyberrealm. Much like the Dream-Zone it's in the Astral Umbra regardless of the fact that humans enter there in their dreams. The only diference was that in First edition the Web was made of Forces instead of Spirit - but that was forgotten in 2.0<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>No, having read the Digital web recently its still made of Forces. Spirits DO slip in but they get in from the Umbra the Infomorphs are the natural residents. Now they aren't really all that different from spirits of those things but I mean chimera aren't all that different from spirits either.<br /> <br /> The difference I was pointing out is the Digital web doesn't follow the whole &quot;Earth overlay&quot;(chimerical reality/Penumbras/Shadowlands) Near(Dreaming/Umbras), Middle and Far/Deep<br /> <br /> SImilarly with the YOmi which re explicitly torn out of the Umbras you don't have They are off in theirown thing, I'd like to see more &quot;off in theirown thing' stuff than this whole Onion reality.<br /> <br /> And more exceptions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T17:31:47-07:00","id":1230692,"title":"","content":"My biggest alteration to Mage cosmology has been that &quot;consensus&quot; and belief impact how magic works. Reality is what it is, but belief influences how the Awakened are able to use magic to manipulate the Tapistry which underlies it. I did this just because it saved me a number of headaches over the years. <br /> <br /> Also, reality is, at times, weird. The Digital Web doesn't exactly conform to anything the Awakened had seen before. And the Hollow Earth is sort of a pocket dimension that exists within the Earth. <br /> <br /> Most of my major chantries are also constructed using Correspondence and other arts to hide them in the material world rather than ever having been in the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T20:23:44-07:00","id":1230732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230692#post1230692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest alteration to Mage cosmology has been that &amp;quot;consensus&amp;quot; and belief impact how magic works. Reality is what it is, but belief influences how the Awakened are able to use magic to manipulate the Tapistry which underlies it. I did this just because it saved me a number of headaches over the years. <br /> <br /> Also, reality is, at times, weird. The Digital Web doesn't exactly conform to anything the Awakened had seen before. And the Hollow Earth is sort of a pocket dimension that exists within the Earth. <br /> <br /> Most of my major chantries are also constructed using Correspondence and other arts to hide them in the material world rather than ever having been in the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I want this. Belief effects reality but reality is old and existed before people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T20:24:29-07:00","id":1230733,"title":"","content":"Also it\u2019s been suggested maybe the digital web sprung from tha location of Mount Qaf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:48:11-07:00","id":1230814,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a rather strong suggestion. Qaf it's mentioned by M20 as the source of the Web.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, having read the Digital web recently its still made of Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that stated or it's a deduction?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits DO slip in but they get in from the Umbra the Infomorphs are the natural residents. Now they aren't really all that different from spirits of those things but I mean chimera aren't all that different from spirits either. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting distinction.<br /> <br /> M20 has Spirits as native, though: See Web Spirits in the spirit hierarchy. Memophores are listed as spirits (minions) created by memes, and have spirit traits. You say Infomorphs aren't very different: I already admited that the Dreaming was an Umbra in everything but name - by that rule of three chimera can't prove Infomorphs aren't spirits...<br /> <br /> Now, can you alter/create/control Infomorphs with Forces alone in Digital Web 2.0?, Are Infomorphs outside Spirit scope the same way animals or humans are?. Because that would be something...I need more than a few cosmetic differences to call something different (and to regret M20 refused to follow that model).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference I was pointing out is the Digital web doesn't follow the whole &quot;Earth overlay&quot;(chimerical reality/Penumbras/Shadowlands) Near(Dreaming/Umbras), Middle and Far/Deep </div> </div> </div>If not being an onion it's all you require to say that a place it's different from the Umbra then every single Realm and Zone follows your requisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-28-2018, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T13:21:00-07:00","id":1230910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230814#post1230814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a rather strong suggestion. Qaf it's mentioned by M20 as the source of the Web.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is that stated or it's a deduction?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the rotes for manipulating them use Spirit, AND they give Gauntlet ratings for various Sector types in the web. Correspondence, Prime, and Forces are considered One level higher for hte mage in the web.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's an interesting distinction.<br /> <br /> M20 has Spirits as native, though: See Web Spirits in the spirit hierarchy. Memophores are listed as spirits (minions) created by memes, and have spirit traits. You say Infomorphs aren't very different: I already admited that the Dreaming was an Umbra in everything but name - by that rule of three chimera can't prove Infomorphs aren't spirits...<br /> <br /> Now, can you alter/create/control Infomorphs with Forces alone in Digital Web 2.0?, Are Infomorphs outside Spirit scope the same way animals or humans are?. Because that would be something...I need more than a few cosmetic differences to call something different (and to regret M20 refused to follow that model). </div> </div> </div>OK here's where it gets complicated. YOu can make a PURE AI that will live in the Digital Web with just Mind... OR you can BIND a spirit into that AI and make into a &quot;Daemon&quot; which is BASICALLY a Fetish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If not being an onion it's all you require to say that a place it's different from the Umbra then every single Realm and Zone follows your requisites. </div> </div> </div>Most Realms I can think of fall into the &quot;onion&quot; paradigm, they are all just shoved somewhere in the middle layer. Stygia, Horizon realms, the various Tribal homelands... now places like Hollow earth have been treated in the past to be sort of a random just side connection like the Digital web.. I wish it would go bakc to that. That there were all sorts of weird places you could get to via wierd means and not &quot;Everything is spirit&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T07:07:58-07:00","id":1231097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> None of the rotes for manipulating them use Spirit, AND they give Gauntlet ratings for various Sector types in the web. Correspondence, Prime, and Forces are considered One level higher for hte mage in the web.</div> </div> </div> </div>That none of the effects that influence the place are Spirit based it's a very good argument - albeit I would have preffered a statement like in 1rst edition. Some Realms influence certain Spheres (Dark Umbra/Entropy ; The Flux/Prime) and some realms do have a Gauntlet (the Shard/Shadow Realms). Still, I can concede the point - the Web, as it can be deduced by it's properties, it's not strictly a place of spirit and it doesn't have to be part of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> That's neat, we need more of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Realms I can think of fall into the &quot;onion&quot; paradigm, they are all just shoved somewhere in the middle layer. Stygia, Horizon realms, the various Tribal homelands... now places like Hollow earth have been treated in the past to be sort of a random just side connection like the Digital web.. I wish it would go bakc to that. That there were all sorts of weird places you could get to via wierd means and not &quot;Everything is spirit&quot; </div> </div> </div>Zones, in the 1rst book about the Umbra (that was from Werewolf), were stated to be places that can be accessed by the Umbra but don't follow the same rules as the Umbra.<br /> <br /> This wasn't explored a lot, but it had potential: Obviously Garou would think that Zones are a part of the Umbra: 1\u00ba because they think everything should be part of the Umbra (Earth it's &quot;The Realm&quot;, after all); 2\u00ba because they have few other means of entering different worlds (and, as the protectors of The Realm, they seldomly need to do that). Mage could have explored all the Zones as trully distinct stuff.<br /> <br /> One thing I liked about CoD it's that the Astral Umbra was accessed from the inside of the mage, and then you were able to access the universal subconscious from your own subconscious - that it's onion-ish indeed but the idea that the first layer it's yourself, and then you go &quot;inwards&quot; to seek the commonplace with humanity it's an interesting distinction, I think.<br /> <br /> Another big deal would have been to explore Outer Space as Outer Space. In the first edition the limits between Umbra and Space weren't clear, as Mage was always picky with the idea that the Void was created by the Void Engineer's Consensual Reality. In Revised Outer Space was outright murdered. However, I find that even if you want OS to have been created by the Consensus (a fact that by all means should be left as a mistery for the ST to decide) it's more ominous to have it as a potentially infinite area rather than a clear and empty boundary - and if it isn't as empty as the Technocracy would want that would only reinforce the idea that they don't control the Consensus as much as they would want to (which should be good for Consensus-theorists, as those who control the Consensus under this theory should be able to redefine all of reality and erase the opposition - Technocrats aren't capable off that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-29-2018, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T16:16:28-07:00","id":1231247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1231097#post1231097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That none of the effects that influence the place are Spirit based it's a very good argument - albeit I would have preffered a statement like in 1rst edition. Some Realms influence certain Spheres (Dark Umbra/Entropy ; The Flux/Prime) and some realms do have a Gauntlet (the Shard/Shadow Realms). Still, I can concede the point - the Web, as it can be deduced by it's properties, it's not strictly a place of spirit and it doesn't have to be part of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> That's neat, we need more of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> My read is from 2.0 which may be completely superceded by 3.0 if its still on the calendar is that its not a realm of spirit. You CAN get there from the Umbra but.. you can get to the material world from the Umbra too. I kind of wish the Dreaming Didn't have spirit requirements to interact with if it was a pure realm of Mind. But maybe I'm getting too COD.<br /> <br /> IF the shard/shade realms had nothing to do with Spirit and Were just accessable and wierd places via spheres Thus why the MATTER Focused SOE are the only people who care about Hollow Earth etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T16:08:11-07:00","id":1231675,"title":"","content":"Id create a way Garou could &quot;Adopt&quot; kin or ordinary humans and confer the garou nature on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T18:36:02-07:00","id":1231705,"title":"","content":"If I could, I'd address the issues involved in the conflicting metaphysics of the gamelines. The Triat, the Judo-Christian God, consensus and reality, the Dreaming and the Umbra, the alternate cosmologies of the KotE and the Ivory Kingdoms, etc.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I wouldn't just hand that info to players but a firm grasp of how it fits together helps a ST keep track of how things could interact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T19:15:37-07:00","id":1231712,"title":"","content":"I feel things could just be less cluttered and themes could feel more cohesive if you condensed the superfluous layers of many, though not all, of the spirit worlds. So Chimera would be the same as the Spirits the Werewolves see. Trods could be the way Changelings differentiate their interaction with the Dreaming, and finally no more dissonance between say the Nunnehi and the Kithain. And the Inanimae all of sudden fit a lot better into the cosmology of other being. They could finally start say popping up in the Middle Kingdom. And maybe have more of an emphasis that while the Triat Exists natural spirits and selfish spirits are free to align themselves how they choose. I would perhaps steal the idea of the Claimed from NWOD and make them a problem seperate from the Fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:22:54-07:00","id":1231767,"title":"","content":"I would mostly want kind of what FallenEco said, but focus mostly on defusing the certanty of WtA lore. Less on the cosmology itself as introducing falsehood, contradictions, and options to the Garou paradigm, which seems to be the main line that causes issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T15:23:25-07:00","id":1231954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1231767#post1231767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would mostly want kind of what FallenEco said, but focus mostly on defusing the certanty of WtA lore. Less on the cosmology itself as introducing falsehood, contradictions, and options to the Garou paradigm, which seems to be the main line that causes issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I use for Garou something who is hinted to be canon. Ancestors don't have perfect memories and any who had Derangements by instance still have it. As for the other spirits the Totems have other things to do than answer questions about history and even their memories are strange and alien.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T16:31:55-07:00","id":1232501,"title":"","content":"I've said these setting hacks many times before, but might as well re-iterate them since it is germane to the topic of the thread.<br /> <br /> I'd get rid of Kuei-Jin and have East Asia dominated by Cainites, and Demon: The Fallen also gets declared non-canon as well.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd get rid of the metaplot in its entirety, and reset everything back to 1E and early 2E. <br /> <br /> If I were in charge of WW, I'd pay the extra money to bring back Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game and integrate it into the World of Darkness, along with Sailor Moon and Highlander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T17:11:40-07:00","id":1232509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1232501#post1232501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said these setting hacks many times before, but might as well re-iterate them since it is germane to the topic of the thread.<br /> <br /> I'd get rid of Kuei-Jin and have East Asia dominated by Cainites, and Demon: The Fallen also gets declared non-canon as well.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd get rid of the metaplot in its entirety, and reset everything back to 1E and early 2E.<br /> <br /> If I were in charge of WW, I'd pay the extra money to bring back Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game and integrate it into the World of Darkness, along with Sailor Moon and Highlander.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> IF we re going that far I'd go so far in the reverse. Make a Completely different Cosmologically incomptable &quot;Vampire&quot; type through out the world.. Wan Kuei, Native American types, Even a STRONG implication Cainites Destroyed the Native European &quot;Vampires&quot; that's why they have such a hate on for &quot;clanless' vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T05:39:41-07:00","id":1232599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1231954#post1231954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I use for Garou something who is hinted to be canon. Ancestors don't have perfect memories and any who had Derangements by instance still have it. As for the other spirits the Totems have other things to do than answer questions about history and even their memories are strange and alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even that so much, as so much of the spiritual side of the Garou's beliefs are fact rather than belief. There is no possibility that totems and spirits could be demons or angels, for instance, or other things than what the Garou know they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T06:44:16-07:00","id":1233976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1232599#post1232599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not even that so much, as so much of the spiritual side of the Garou's beliefs are fact rather than belief. There is no possibility that totems and spirits could be demons or angels, for instance, or other things than what the Garou know they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. Personally that doesn't disturb me because the other games have spirits and ghosts be simply things that exist in the world.<br /> <br /> Now Ga\u00efa (and perhaps the heavy hitters of the cosmology) could totally be something else. Demon the Fallen talk about the Werewolves being Angelic Creation and Ga\u00efa being the Seraph of the Sixth House. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T07:05:48-07:00","id":1233986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230042#post1230042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use a weird allegory, cWoD is like piling a bunch of fantasy books on to of one another, it is dense and the more you have to make sure it doesn't fall over. NWoD is like legos, sure you can build it like the instructions, or you can build what you like. I love the setting of cWoD a lot, but I prefer the looser worldbuilding since it is easier to wing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I finally wrapped my head around WHY I have a huge preference for cWoD over nWoD/CofD: I <b>hate</b> Legos! Seriously, building with them, using instructions or not, gives me anxiety. I guess maybe the uniformity of the pieces in the chaos bothers me in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:23:13-07:00","id":1236536,"title":"","content":"Personally. i like to think that God pulled a doctor manhattan and other beings had to take her role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T20:16:27-07:00","id":1236660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1236536#post1236536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally. i like to think that God pulled a doctor manhattan and other beings had to take her role.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So someone traveled back in time that caused a universe reboot and God showed up and took out a sizable period of time because she thought it was funny?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:34:00-07:00","id":1237000,"title":"","content":"Honestly I really don't see a problem with the WOD cosmology. The Meta-Plot have many strange story elements that conflict, run in circles, or leave off in dead ends sure, but the cosmology is Supposed to be far beyond any one group.<br /> <br /> IF all the settings are cannon, it really puts effort on the storyteller to try to balance the different tones of each game. They aren't necessary though. However if you include everything, the setting becomes bigger than any group will tell you, Big bads stop be &quot;The BIG BAD&quot; and become &quot;one of the Big Bads&quot;, history becomes muddled and full of inconsistent viewpoints(a lot like real history honestly), and many of the different splats are just Wrong at some points(which kinda humanizes them). <br /> <br /> The biggest change I'd make though is information available about different factions, the Camerilla can't Really be unaware that pentex or the technocracy exist or vise versa without making them all seem incompetent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T06:15:35-07:00","id":1237110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1237000#post1237000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest change I'd make though is information available about different factions, the Camerilla can't Really be unaware that pentex or the technocracy exist or vise versa without making them all seem incompetent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's one of the greatest WTF? of crossoverland. Major supernatural forces that supposedly &quot;rule the night&quot; can't possibly be irrelevant to each other. To say: &quot;yeah, we know there are other mysterious beings out there, but we only know rumors about them and they're largely unimportant&quot; strains the suspension of disbelieve. Eventually their so called areas of influence overlap and they do have conflicts of interest. <br /> <br /> Best solution it's to say that humans are the ones who trully rule the night and big supernatural organizations opperate like huge mafias that like to think they have more influence than they really have but know well that the others exist and do have to deal with them if they cross the line. That way you don't have to think about who owns the world between the big three.<br /> <br /> TheTe chnocratic answer to the Sabbat can't be &quot;oh well, the Camarilla have them under control so there's no problem here. Better concentrate the majority of our resource on oppressing the hippie terrorists&quot;, if they trully care about protecting humanity. This makes them look either incompetent or cynic beyond redemption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:38:42-07:00","id":1237313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1237110#post1237110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> TheTe chnocratic answer to the Sabbat can't be &quot;oh well, the Camarilla have them under control so there's no problem here. Better concentrate the majority of our resource on oppressing the hippie terrorists&quot;, if they trully care about protecting humanity. This makes them look either incompetent or cynic beyond redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or PROFOUNDLY egocentric. &quot;One mage is worth countless vampires..:&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:37:00-07:00","id":1237333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1237313#post1237313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or PROFOUNDLY egocentric. &quot;One mage is worth countless vampires..:&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So outfit sleepers with awakened devices?<br /> <br /> If you look at the mechanics of charm and artifact production, a mage with the right backgrounds(namely sanctum and cult) can easily have items with 20+ successes to effect that they can carry in mass. Combine with factory production techniques, the fact the technocracy owns a massive number of nodes, has an incentive to trade materials between location/the means to do so easily(correspondence), and the fact that large collectives of scientists working on large projects is the norm rather than the exception, and what you end up with is an organization Designed to pump out powerful &quot;magic&quot; items with an obscene number of available sphere effects on such a mind crushing scale it really starts to make sense why they crushed the old Wizard-Kings or times passed.(also of note: whether or not wonders can be made autonomously by other, specially made wonders, should be considered. Say you create a special fire spirit fetish thats only function is to imbue items with the ability to cast fireballs and hook it up to a supply of quint. This question hasn't been addressed anywhere I've looked though, so it's up to the storyteller)<br /> <br /> It's kinda the reason I run my crossover games with the technocrats enforcing the veil/masquerade/supernatural secrecy thing, as they can outfit teams of regular mortals with enough hyper-advanced mundane tech, awakened equipment, and cybernetic/genetic enhancements that they can temporarily compete with supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:41:09-07:00","id":1237334,"title":"","content":"It's a non-issue because of the different game lines being about different things. In a game featuring Mages and Vampires you;re more likely to find the technocracy taking a more active hand than you're ever likely to see in a Vampire centric game, unless the ST chooses otherwise. Conversely in a Technocracy game you may very well find yourself up against vampire and Werewolves as well as Mages because that can be a game focus, but in a Traditions or Ascension War themed game the other supernaturals have basically zero impact. <br /> <br /> The Union doesn't care so much about 'protecting humanity' as 'maintaining reality' with the single biggest threat to the consensus being Mages as unlike shifters and vampires which are untidy fragments of a neat consensus Mages actively threaten to break the whole gig. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla probably are aware of Pentex (or more specifically some Vampire from some of the Clans are because the Cam is hardly an actual Organisation rather an alliance of City States) and just don't care because they're just another corporation as far as most of them are concerned. Infact many of the Cam elders probably make the average Pentex activity seem nice by comparison. If the Syndicate put any stock is 'spirits' or even 'dimensional sciences' as anything other than a splinter fringe of space exploration and paid more attention to the Void Engineers they may actually care more about Pentex. But they don't. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't mess around with the WoD cosmology because to do so means making compromises between the games that doesn't really add anything to any of the and takes something away from them too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T18:53:28-07:00","id":1237358,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Prometheas;n1237333]<br /> <br /> So outfit sleepers with awakened devices?<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<br /> <br /> they do.. that's what they send to deal with most Traditon threats. Either the Traditions are enough of a legitimate Threat for the Technocracy... or they are profoundly incompitent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T08:13:56-07:00","id":1237967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1237334#post1237334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a non-issue because of the different game lines being about different things. In a game featuring Mages and Vampires you;re more likely to find the technocracy taking a more active hand than you're ever likely to see in a Vampire centric game, unless the ST chooses otherwise. Conversely in a Technocracy game you may very well find yourself up against vampire and Werewolves as well as Mages because that can be a game focus, but in a Traditions or Ascension War themed game the other supernaturals have basically zero impact.<br /> <br /> The Union doesn't care so much about 'protecting humanity' as 'maintaining reality' with the single biggest threat to the consensus being Mages as unlike shifters and vampires which are untidy fragments of a neat consensus Mages actively threaten to break the whole gig.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet we see Vampires and Pentex regularly do stuff that would make any mage a primary target for the Technocracy in a Mage game w/o consequences. Things like massive blood cults and/or releasing sanity shattering monsters that make the &quot;fireball in an open street&quot; seem tame by comparison. Yet the Technocracy doesn't show up.<br /> <br /> For instance, a bunch of Techno-Anarchs caused the last world spanning financial crisis in V20 continuity. If a mage did something like that, the Syndicate would show up because it's their job - yet they aren't mentioned. Guess if it's vampires it's alright, Reality it's safe and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't mess around with the WoD cosmology because to do so means making compromises between the games that doesn't really add anything to any of the and takes something away from them too. </div> </div> </div>WoD cosmology already does that. Unless you don't use crossover, of course","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T19:32:59-07:00","id":1238110,"title":"","content":"Yep, because one is using a static part of actual reality to do it, the other is literally reshaping reality, to whit ripping apart the Tapestry and folding it back in a new form, to generate the same effects. Mages are a target because they use Sphere Magick, it's not what they do it's how they do it and that they exist at all. <br /> <br /> Most people don't seem to do a lot of crossover from a play perspective and it only seems to come in when a ST wants to change up the adversaries and allies that may be around for a player group, at which point it's up to the ST what they want to use and not use and how they want things to mesh. The WoD isn't designed to be a one world of darkness, but it's not hard to make things work together. Want Mage and Vampire (Blood Treachery) to be your central games in a crossover, no problem, the Technocratic Union respond to Vampire stuff more often maybe, or maybe the Masquerade is perhaps that effective that only a few technocrats even pay heed to the Vampire stuff at all, thinking that there's only a couple here and there. <br /> <br /> Also it's worth noting that Mages tend to use the High Umbra, Garou the Middle Umbra (along with Dreamspeakers, with the VE's tending to be out past the Horizon in the Aetherial Realms) and Vampires when they have a connection the Dark Umbra or Shadowlands (along with Wraiths) the Cosmology fits fine. heck Infinite Tapestry talks at length about the possibilities of Umbral realms without really defining them where Werewolf defines them and most of the books that did that defining were Werewolf &amp; Mage source books (Axis Mundi, Book of the Weaver, Umbra didnt carry the mage tag but mentions Dreamspeakers and a few other mages and some of the Mage books reference the Umbra book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T11:07:00-07:00","id":1238285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1237967#post1237967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet we see Vampires and Pentex regularly do stuff that would make any mage a primary target for the Technocracy in a Mage game w/o consequences. Things like massive blood cults and/or releasing sanity shattering monsters that make the &quot;fireball in an open street&quot; seem tame by comparison. Yet the Technocracy doesn't show up.<br /> <br /> For instance, a bunch of Techno-Anarchs caused the last world spanning financial crisis in V20 continuity. If a mage did something like that, the Syndicate would show up because it's their job - yet they aren't mentioned. Guess if it's vampires it's alright, Reality it's safe and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the anarchs claim they did it. the Syndicate claims that it was a massive paradox backlash on the Technocracy from recent events..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T13:41:49-07:00","id":1238350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1238110#post1238110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, because one is using a static part of actual reality to do it, the other is literally reshaping reality, to whit ripping apart the Tapestry and folding it back in a new form, to generate the same effects. Mages are a target because they use Sphere Magick, it's not what they do it's how they do it and that they exist at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm...no. The Technocracy never ever states that their intended purpose it's &quot;to protect the world from sphere magick&quot;. The Consensus isn't informed by sphere magick, the Consensus it's informed by Belief. Technocracy cares about these transgresions. And the Syndicate, as per the bible, had a lot of trouble with that particular crisis - it made them look pretty bad with the rest Conventions just when the NWO it's menacing a civil war against them.<br /> <br /> Being a Technocrat isn't about protecting humanity?. Yet they babble about them doing that thouzands of times (unsung heros and all that). But even if you want to see the fine print on the Precepts of Damian and say that you're not forced to protect the masses, just to keep them ignorant, then you're still forced to admit that such protection of the Consensus it's about controling belief, not about controling dynamic magick. And mages don't have a monopoly on that<br /> <br /> What you say it's a perfect example of how you can force things into making sense by making compromises between the games that doesn't really add anything to any of the and takes something away from them too:<br /> <br /> Now It makes sense that the Technocracy doesn't hunt supers, but you're making a compromise: All that talk about &quot;protecting the masses&quot;? - propaganda. All that talk about belief? - nonsense. The Technocracy regulates the use Dynamic Magick, that's what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most people don't seem to do a lot of crossover from a play perspective and it only seems to come in when a ST wants to change up the adversaries and allies that may be around for a player group, at which point it's up to the ST what they want to use and not use and how they want things to mesh. The WoD isn't designed to be a one world of darkness, but it's not hard to make things work together. Want Mage and Vampire (Blood Treachery) to be your central games in a crossover, no problem, the Technocratic Union respond to Vampire stuff more often maybe, or maybe the Masquerade is perhaps that effective that only a few technocrats even pay heed to the Vampire stuff at all, thinking that there's only a couple here and there. </div> </div> </div>I agree. To MAKE them go together it's relatively easy. By doing that you're necessarily making compromises between the games that, most of the time, take something away from them.<br /> <br /> You've provided the perfect example above with a Technocracy that acts like Paradox Spirits, only caring about Dynamic powers while ignoring the betterment of humanity - a lot of Mage fans would not be OK with that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-24-2018, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T13:48:09-07:00","id":1238353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1238285#post1238285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the anarchs claim they did it. the Syndicate claims that it was a massive paradox backlash on the Technocracy from recent events..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure. But that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> If the first claim it's true then the Syndicate should be furious with them and taking action. If the second it's true, it makes sense with Mage and doesn't contradict Vampire (anarchs always claim stuff) ... but it erases an option to create stories that was left for Vampire. That's the price of having a setting that makes sense for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T14:29:52-07:00","id":1238370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1238353#post1238353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, sure. But that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> If the first claim it's true then the Syndicate should be furious with them and taking action. If the second it's true, it makes sense with Mage and doesn't contradict Vampire (anarchs always claim stuff) ... but it erases an option to create stories that was left for Vampire. That's the price of having a setting that makes sense for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST you have the option for both. Most supernaturals are profoundly arrogant and consider themselves the sole cause, if two people are working towards something and it ends up happening both claim to be the sole cause when it wouldn't have happened without either.. though it may have happen without either!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T15:18:29-07:00","id":1238384,"title":"","content":"Ironically enough, the great depression could also have been an event that was bound to happen do to human error and the fact people at the time didn't understand or respect how delicate economic balance is. Looking at the history of the actual event, a lot more factors went into it than can be pushed on to one group or the other, even if in WOD both the Anarchs and syndicate contributed significantly.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure both groups in a One WOD setting can be convinced they or some other nebulous are solely to blame, but reality is more complex then that. It's entirely possible that the economy crashed do to various different kinds of abuse(both magical and mundane) by different groups, and when things fell through everyone started pointing fingers(a lot like in real life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T03:52:58-07:00","id":1238544,"title":"","content":"I think you are misconstruing Aleph. <br /> <br /> Yes the Technocratic Union is about &quot;Protecting Humanity &amp; Reality from the Things&quot; but this is covered in the front of the Guide to the Technocracy where it presents the single biggest threat to the world being Reality Deviants and the biggest threat to the Union (given the Ascension War for one thing) are the Reality Deviants of the Traditions. <br /> It then goes on to talk about the other supernaturals and the problem they have with dealing with them coming down to manpower, intel and even parts of the union accepting that things like the Walking Dead and Shapeshifters exist. <br /> <br /> It also comes down to how BIG you want the Union to be I suppose and what it's immediate, far reaching and true agendas are, because whenever the Union is brought up in these discussions as the hammer that smacks supernaturals that is an actual problem. While most of the Conventions have 'field agents' a lot of what people are thinking of is not what the Conventions deploy. You have a limited number of MiB clones, a more limited number of HiTmarks, only so many MiB-MiG-MiW Enlightened Agents from within the NWO and only so many Void Engineer marines you can drop in. They do have a lot of 'mundane' agents and operatives for a given value of 'a lot' in the same way that say the FBI has a lot of field agents. This is why from the outside when you come up against the Union they are a Conspiracy Theory with a few Agents in Mirrorshades and some local law enforcement back up who may also have a specialist SWAT team and a Terminator if things get REALLY bad. <br /> <br /> Don't forget that, with crossover 'numbers' supplied Mages are rarer than Garou to something like 1-5 and the Union has, at best really half of the Mages in the world, where as the Garou have over 90% of the Garou in the world. The Garou are in a more open war with the agencies of Pentex (given that few of them will actually know Pentex itself) that's been going on for over 100 years now and Pentex has gotten stronger and more nebulous. The Union is in a more or less open war with the other half of the Mages in reality and a bunch of the dark nasty stuff that's in space and they attempt to get involved when supernatural stuff happens (because we are told they do) even with some of them not believing in it AND they do not want any of Humanity finding out what they've been dealing with, except for those few directly linked to the Union and even then they probably do psychological things to them (Mind effects). Not to mention they love their internal red tape and they are not quite as omniscient as they would have everyone believe. This is all while their membership as a whole are working through their Genius to grow and learn (because an Avatar doesn't stop being an Avatar that drives a Mage to new heights just because it's a technocrat) and you want to keep your membership happy, or at least compliant, else they could go rogue (or worse Marauder or Nephandic given the right circumstances). Plus the Union itself wishes to remain hidden. <br /> <br /> This is why you get the &quot;Vampires police their own&quot; from the departments that don't just assume it's a drug deal gone bad when they hear about a monstrous killing. Why their not kicking down the door of every Pentex subsidiary and why they are not always chasing after reports of urban 'bear' attacks. But they are VERY concerned about the people who want the Consensus to change, don't have real issues with revealing to parts of the world that Science isn't all there is. This is also why they ARE an interesting antagonist to throw into another splat's game on occasion because part of that is looking at WHY they have shown up, what part of the global conspiracy have the characters inadvertently stumbled upon or upset. Nothing needs to be altered in this case, because it rides off the back of how things are; when the Vampire coterie helped the wrong mortal, or killed the wrong person, or influenced an affair and suddenly have the MiB tracking them. Maybe the garou pack destroys a Weaver facility with a supposedly harmful product, not knowing it was a Lab (or attached to) of the Progenitors who were dealing with an issue that could wipe out that town or city so the NWO requests aid from the Void Engineers and Iteration X and suddenly the pack have HITmarks and Power Armoured umbral adversaries to deal with and again it's all par the course for what's already written rather than having to re-imagine things. <br /> <br /> OR you play a Union game and stumble across some of the Pentex stuff you'd normally only see in Werewolf and all the threads you could use from that, maybe there is internal corruption with the local Syndicate that's support this subsidiary, maybe someone has gone Malfaen Nephandi, maybe because a lot of the Pentex stuff is actually quite covert themselves and that they are killing local supernatural oppositions (Vampire AND Garou) without being obvious themselves AND that their business is good for local economy (and therefore human well being, for a given value) any side effects are being written off or let slide because there are bigger threats and issues on the plate. This even works in a Traditions game but I think is more fun when applied from a Union character PoV). Your not taking anything away or even changing anything when things are used this way. <br /> <br /> In fact the existing scope for using the tools of the different games as they stand is rather broad, the cosmologies (which is the spirit world affairs their of) fit with minimal work if any around the core games. Game mechanics are the trickier side of things but there is advice there too. <br /> <br /> I think, in relation to the OP's question (the intended one anyway). Is still that I wouldn't change any of the Cosmology but I think it's a worth while look at how to use the extant information, splats, game lines and settings in a cross over capacity for the best new story ideas, twists on classic story ideas and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T10:35:52-07:00","id":1238979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1230692#post1230692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest alteration to Mage cosmology has been that &quot;consensus&quot; and belief impact how magic works. Reality is what it is, but belief influences how the Awakened are able to use magic to manipulate the Tapistry which underlies it. I did this just because it saved me a number of headaches over the years.<br /> <br /> Also, reality is, at times, weird. The Digital Web doesn't exactly conform to anything the Awakened had seen before. And the Hollow Earth is sort of a pocket dimension that exists within the Earth.<br /> <br /> Most of my major chantries are also constructed using Correspondence and other arts to hide them in the material world rather than ever having been in the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I've used this for a while. Belief *molds* reality, but it doesn't *create* it. There are so many things wrong with how MtA presents consensual reality that can be fixed with this simple shift in the premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}